{
  "comment": "Same plugin-panel pattern as the tg55/d110 layouts. Rows follow the 4-op FM voice: voice common (algorithm, OP4 feedback, transpose, pseudo-reverb, poly/mono, bend) + LFO -> operator (frequency/wave/level) -> operator EG -> operator scaling/sensitivity/mute -> voice function (wheel, portamento, breath, foot). All operator groups share one select var {o} (select.shared = 'op', 'all' writes all four operators). Frequency is coarse + fine: in ratio mode the LCD ratio is tx81z.json freqTables.ratio[crs][fine] (crs 4 fine 0 = 1.00); in fixed mode Hz = (((crs & 0x3C) << 2) + fine + (crs < 4 ? 8 : 0)) << range; the knobs show raw numbers until the editor learns display 'tx81zFreqCoarse'. EG is Yamaha 4-op rate/level (AR, D1R, D1L, D2R, RR; rates 0-31 fast = high, RR 1-15), so plain knobs, not an env cell. OP1's EG shift is fixed off. The TX81Z has no pitch EG (VCED 87-92 are DX21-only); the 'reverb rate' is an EG-release trick, not an effect. 'on' toggles are live operator mutes (not stored). Sustain/portamento/chorus switch bits are stored but have no panel page and are left off the faceplate. The voice name is edited in the name field (name1-10).",
